# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Authority material is large and content-addressed. The registry
# (forensics/authorities/AUTHORITIES.json) IS checked in, because it is the
# evidence that binds claims to hashes. The per-file SOURCE_MANIFEST.*.json is
# also checked in: it is tamper-evidence for the extracted source tree, so that
# the recorded root hash is verifiable without re-downloading. Only the
# archives, extracted trees, build directories and installed prefixes are
# reproducible-and-ignored.
/forensics/authorities/downloads/
/forensics/authorities/src/
/forensics/authorities/build/
/forensics/authorities/prefix/
/forensics/authorities/captures/

# Court scratch material produced inside the container.
/court/

# Phase 2 distribution shell: the bulky artifacts are generated and reproducible
# from forensics/tools/build_phase2.sh (the version scripts, pkg-config metadata,
# shell manifest and court results ARE committed as evidence).
/artifacts/phase2/*.so
/artifacts/phase2/*.so.*
/artifacts/phase2/*.a
/artifacts/phase2/include/
/artifacts/phase2/shell/

# Gemel's evidence-native store. Gemel ships its OWN `.gemel/.gitignore`
# containing `*`, so the store is excluded from git BY DESIGN: it is meant to be
# synced through Gemel's own mechanisms (`gemel remote` / `push` / `exchange`)
# and projected into git deterministically with `gemel export-git` (Phase 4),
# not committed raw. This project respects that rather than fighting it with
# `git add -f`.
#
# What IS committed is the legible projection at forensics/GEMEL_TRAJECTORY.md,
# generated from `gemel log` / `gemel status`, plus the change, trajectory and
# checkpoint identities recorded in docs/ and the seal. The store itself is
# local working evidence; if a future phase wants it in git, the honest route is
# `gemel export-git`, not a forced commit of 95 MB of content-addressed blobs.
#
# FRF is the opposite case and IS committed: `.frf` carries the claim-bearing
# receipts and claims, and FRF expects them to travel.

# FRF's portable OpenReceipt bundles are DERIVED exports of the committed .frf
# store (each ~20 MB: the closure includes the snapshotted authority DSOs).
# They are reproducible from the documented command, so they are not duplicated
# in git; the store they export from is committed.
/forensics/frf/bundles/

# Editor / OS noise
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Python bytecode. Generated interpreter state must never sit beside forensic
# tooling: it is not evidence, it is not reproducible, and in a project whose
# whole claim is reproducibility it is actively misleading.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Scratch material used to splice source in place. Two of these were committed by
# accident in the Phase 5.3 merge (`forensics/.d2i_head.rs`, `forensics/.d2i_tail.rs`)
# because they were in the working tree at `git add -A` time. A dot-prefixed file
# under `forensics/` is never evidence, so the whole shape is excluded rather than
# the two names.
/forensics/.*.rs

# Commit-message and scratch files edited to a dot-prefixed name so they sort first,
# then swept in by `git add -A`. The same accident as the two `.rs` splice files
# above, one directory up: a dot-prefixed file at the repository root is never
# evidence, so the shape is excluded rather than the names.
.*.tmp
